/** @page yamlreleasehistory yaml Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section yaml_bundled_3_0 Qore 3.0

    - bundled the native YAML module and all twelve user modules with Qore
    - fixed overflow when parsing timestamps with more than six fractional-second digits
    - added cancellation checks to scalar scanning and merge expansion

    <b>New Features</b>
    - added @ref Qore::YAML::parse_yaml(string, int) "parse_yaml(string, int)" and the
      @ref yaml_parse_option_constants "YAML::ParseCoreSchema" option, which resolves plain scalars with the
      YAML 1.2 core schema only, so JSON-compatible documents written by other tools (such as OpenAPI
      descriptions) keep values such as \c 2025-03-05T14:59:25Z and \c PT as strings instead of converting them
      to dates
    - added @ref Qore::YAML::YamlSaxParser "YamlSaxParser" class for SAX-style event-based YAML
      parsing with proper value deserialization
    - added @ref Qore::YAML::YamlDocumentIterator "YamlDocumentIterator" class for iterating
      multi-document YAML streams
    - added @ref Qore::YAML::YamlStreamWriter "YamlStreamWriter" class for streaming YAML output
    - added @ref Qore::YAML::YamlSaxEventType "YamlSaxEventType" and
      @ref Qore::YAML::YamlScalarStyle "YamlScalarStyle" enums
    - added @ref Qore::YAML::YamlSaxEvent "YamlSaxEvent" hashdecl for SAX event data

    <b>New User Modules</b>
    - added <a href="../../YamlRpcClientIo/html/index.html">YamlRpcClientIo</a>:
      pure-Qore YAML-RPC client with async I/O via \c HttpClientIo; this is the async I/O
      replacement for the \c YamlRpcClient module, providing the same YAML-RPC call API
      with automatic HTTP/3, HTTP/2, and HTTP/1.1 protocol negotiation and connection pooling
      - \c yamlrpcio:// and \c yamlrpcios:// URL schemes for ConnectionProvider
    - added <a href="../../Connect/html/index.html">Connect</a>: Connect RPC protocol
      module implementing DataStream 2.0 with YAML as the primary codec; supports unary,
      server-streaming, client-streaming, and bidirectional-streaming RPC patterns over
      HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, and HTTP/3
      - standard 5-byte framed envelopes compatible with gRPC tooling
      - extensible codec system via \c AbstractConnectCodec
      - JSON codec (\c JsonConnectCodec) for JSON serialization
      - CBOR codec (\c CborConnectCodec) for compact binary serialization (RFC 8949),
        using the bundled \c json module
      - per-message compression for streaming RPCs (\c gzip and \c deflate)
      - automatic compression negotiation via \c connect-content-encoding and
        \c connect-accept-encoding headers
      - conditional gRPC and gRPC-Web interoperability when the \c grpc module is available
      - Connect protocol error model with 16 status codes matching gRPC semantics
      - \c GrpcDetection utility class for gRPC/gRPC-Web content-type detection and
        \c grpc-timeout header parsing (always available, no \c grpc module dependency)
      - HTTP/3 (QUIC) transport with 0-RTT and connection migration support
    - added <a href="../../ConnectDataProvider/html/index.html">ConnectDataProvider</a>:
      DataProvider and ConnectionProvider integration for the Connect RPC protocol
      - factory registered as \c "connect" in the DataProvider framework
      - \c connect:// (plaintext) and \c connects:// (TLS) URL schemes for ConnectionProvider
      - hierarchical provider: root → service → method with dynamic child creation
      - unary RPC via \c doRequest() on method-level providers
    - added <a href="../../YamlDocumentDataProvider/html/index.html">YamlDocumentDataProvider</a>:
      data provider for reading multi-document YAML streams
    - added <a href="../../YamlSchema/html/index.html">YamlSchema</a>: YAML schema validation
    - added <a href="../../YamlTagHandler/html/index.html">YamlTagHandler</a>: custom YAML tag handling

    <b>Improvements</b>
    - <a href="../../DataStreamUtil/html/index.html">DataStreamUtil</a>: added Connect protocol
      (DataStream 2.0) framing utility functions: \c connect_frame_message(),
      \c connect_unframe_message(), \c connect_next_frame_size(),
      \c connect_detect_protocol(), \c connect_get_send(), \c connect_get_recv(),
      \c connect_set_chunked_headers(), \c connect_set_non_chunked_headers();
      added \c CONNECT_DEFAULT_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE constant (4 MB default, matching gRPC)
    - <a href="../../DataStreamClient/html/index.html">DataStreamClient</a>: added Connect
      protocol (DataStream 2.0) support with auto-negotiation; the client tries Connect mode
      first (over HTTP/2 or HTTP/3) and falls back to DataStream v1 if the server doesn't
      support Connect; new constructor options:
      \c protocol (\c "auto", \c "connect", \c "datastream") and \c http3_protocol
      (\c "auto", \c "h2", \c "h3"); new methods: \c setProtocol(), \c getProtocol(),
      \c getDetectedProtocol(), \c resetProtocolCache()
    - <a href="../../DataStreamRequestHandler/html/index.html">DataStreamRequestHandler</a>:
      added automatic Connect protocol (DataStream 2.0) detection; the handler now accepts
      both Connect-framed and DataStream v1 chunked requests without any changes to subclasses;
      added \c isConnectProtocol() method to query the detected protocol
    - added \c %strict-args compile-time requirement to all user modules
    - added debug logging support with <tt>@@debug()</tt> to YamlRpcHandler, YamlRpcClient,
      DataStreamClient, and DataStreamRequestHandler modules
    - added <tt>@@assert()</tt> statements for input validation
    - added documentation for \c DataStreamDeserializationSupport and related constants

    <b>Bug Fixes</b>
    - fixed document float serialization producing invalid scalars such as \c 1e+09.0 and losing
      significant digits; finite floats now round trip exactly, including signed zero and values
      outside the integer range, using the fewest of 15, 16, or 17 significant digits that do (so \c 99.99
      stays \c 99.99), and non-finite floats use standard YAML spellings
    - fixed scalar resolution silently converting digit-free tokens such as \c . and \c .e3 to zero;
      malformed exponents and malformed Qore numeric suffixes now remain strings
    - added YAML \c .inf and \c .nan spellings, including their specified case variants, to implicit
      resolution and explicit \c !!float parsing; invalid explicitly tagged floats now raise a parser error
      instead of converting a partial value or aborting on empty input
    - fixed implicit type resolution incorrectly converting literal and folded block scalar text to other types
    - fixed implicit type resolution converting plain scalars that only look like ISO 8601 durations to a zero
      duration: \c P, \c PT (the country code of Portugal), and \c P1DT have no duration component or no time
      component after \c T and now remain strings, so plain country code lists in documents such as OpenAPI
      schemas keep their values
    - fixed an emitter bug where date-only timestamps whose day ended in \c '0' were
      truncated by an unconditional \c trim_trailing('0') intended only for the
      microseconds component (e.g. \c "2026-04-10" was emitted as \c "2026-04-1"); the
      fractional-seconds trim is now skipped when the formatted string contains no decimal
      point, so date-only values round-trip exactly
    - fixed errno handling in integer parsing (was set after \c strtoll instead of before)
    - fixed error message in YAML parser to show proper line/column and error description

    @section yaml_1_0_0 yaml Module Version 1.0.0
    - fixed a bug parsing single-quoted date-only strings (ex: \c '2022-02-22'), previously parsed as date/time
      values, now parsed correctly as strings
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4914">issue 4914</a>)
    - fixed a bug parsing <tt>'n'</tt>; was parsed to \c 0n before, now parsed correctly
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4894">issue 4893</a>)
    - fixed a bug where aliases in YAML caused parsing to fail
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4891">issue 4891</a>)

    @section yaml073 yaml Module Version 0.7.3
    - updated to build with \c qpp from %Qore 1.12.4+

    @section yaml072 yaml Module Version 0.7.2
    - improved deserialization of date/time values; fixed a bug where a random string could be deserialized as a
      duration
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4642">issue 4642</a>)

    @section yaml071 yaml Module Version 0.7.1
    - fixed a bug where REST schema validation was not applied in the
      <a href="../../DataStreamClient/html/index.html">DataStreamClient</a> module with non-DataStream messages
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4518">issue 4518</a>)

    @section yaml07 yaml Module Version 0.7

    - fixed a bug deserializing implicit string values in some cases
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4241">issue 4241</a>)
    - fixed a bug where serialization errors in YAML-RPC responses would cause a confusing response to be returned
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4194">issue 4194</a>)
    - implemented support for serializing connection objects
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3696">issue 3696</a>)
    - fixed parsing XML in XML encoded responses
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3587">issue 3587</a>)
    - fixed the return types of deserializtion to avoid type stripping
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3432">issue 3432</a>)
    - fixed output of excess noise in floating-point values
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3375">issue 3375</a>)
    - fixed a bug in the <a href="../../DataStreamClient/html/index.html">DataStreamClient</a> module where the
      \c "response-code" key of the info output hash could be missing in some cases
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3237">issue 3237</a>)
    - added optional support for serializing SQL NULL values with @ref Qore::YAML::EmitSqlNull "EmitSqlNull"
    - updated the <a href="../../YamlRpcClient/html/index.html">YamlRpcClient</a> module to support the updated
      abstract connection API (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/2628">issue 2628</a>)

    @section yaml06 yaml Module Version 0.6

    - fixed a bug where strings with invalid encodings were being emitted as-is in exception strings
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3394">issue 3394</a>)
    - improved the description for the \c DESERIALIZATION-ERROR exception for non-deserializable message bodies from
      HTTP servers with error responses (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/1033">issue 1033</a>)
    - added the \c YamlRpcConnection class to the <a href="../../YamlRpcClient/html/index.html">YamlRpcClient</a>
      module
    - updated the <a href="../../DataStreamClient/html/index.html">DataStreamClient</a> module for complex types and
      new internal RestClient API changes (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/2073">issue 2073</a>)
    - updated the <a href="../../DataStreamUtil/html/index.html">DataStreamUtil</a> module for complex types
    - fixed a bug deserializing single-quoted strings; also serialized \c "!number" values will always include the tag
      to avoid potential future ambiguity (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/2343">issue 2343</a>)
    - improved argument error messages with RPC calls in the
      <a href="../../YamlRpcHandler/html/index.html">YamlRpcHandler</a> module
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/2573">issue 2573</a>)

